{
  "$comment": [
    "THE SCREEN MANIFEST — every distinct screen and state prototype v7 can render.",
    "",
    "Built by reading docs/design/command-center-v7/AFS_Command_Center_Prototype_v7.html in full:",
    "its render() dispatcher (line 1207), every page function, every modalHTML() branch,",
    "and every state field in seed()'s OUT object that changes what is on screen.",
    "",
    "WHY IT IS A FILE AND NOT A LIST IN A TEST. A state missing from the manifest is a",
    "state nobody checks. Writing it down separately from the harness means the",
    "enumeration can be reviewed against the prototype on its own, and the harness",
    "fails loudly (`manifest entry has no steps`) rather than quietly skipping.",
    "",
    "DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED, with reasons:",
    "  - #gpeek (the hover-enlarge preview). It is reachable only by a real pointer",
    "    hovering a [data-pid]/[data-job] element, and its POSITION is computed from",
    "    the hovered element's viewport rectangle. A full-page screenshot of a",
    "    hover-positioned fixed overlay is not reproducible, and the brief asks for",
    "    hover-independent states.",
    "  - #toast. A 6.5-second timer overlay; it is state, but it is time-dependent and",
    "    carries no layout of its own beyond one line of text.",
    "  - document.requestFullscreen() in A.opFull. Headless Chromium grants it",
    "    inconsistently; the `op-full` entry below exercises S.opFull instead, which is",
    "    what actually changes the markup.",
    "",
    "`protoSteps` are executed against the untouched prototype. `liveSteps` against the",
    "app in fixture mode. `liveRoute: null` means NO live route exists for this state —",
    "the harness records it as MISSING rather than passing it by omission."
  ],
